sts, so I can't confirm the poem's author, headnote, or exact text from them.\n\nThe poem itself reads roughly as: if I keep remembering the vows we exchanged through the night, I will long for you and shed tears, and I'd want to see the color of those tears. That's my own paraphrase, not a sourced reading.\n\nFor reliable details, I'd try a search on 後拾遺集 哀傷 with the author's name or the headnote (詞書), or a database such as 和歌データベース (Kokka Database) or the National Institute of Japanese Literature's collections, which list poem text, author, and section."], "durationSeconds": 7.922683125, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01R13eCF4Cs15Ar6e2g3TTJX", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
